Pets sometimes DO step into maps, just to make it possible for them to
follow their master, but normally they mostly avoid any kind of traps, even
ones that don't harm them at all.
When I find a map in a narrow corridor in the mines, so that you can't
walk around it, I normally use a pick-axe / mattock or a wand of digging
to make an opening in the wall next to the map, to make it possible to
walk around without stepping in the map.
This makes it easier for pets to follow, and it is also necessary for the
_ (travel) command to find the route.
Whenever there is a monster digging tunnels, it probably has a pick-axe or
a mattock. One can often be found somewhere in the mines.

